Z||000007||JSocha||08-28-2001||04:53 PM||||FYI: As a manager fierobaby, you do have the right to know what the grounds were for your dismissal, including all documentation that are in and part of "your" employee file.<P>If one of my employees were terminated and comes in here and asks for a copy of his file, we are obligated to give it to him and go over and make copies while he is there.  <P>At your request, and do this ONLY when you are there...do not call them to have them make copies, be there when they do, or take the file yourself and make a complete copy and return the employment file...as they are required to give you all paper work in YOUR file.  By being there, this ensures you that they do not slip something in that you are unaware of or afterwards unbenounced to you as a reason for your dismissal, or take documents out (such as an employee appraisal/review, job performance, reason for recent raises, requests for time off, etc.).<P>And if he says he has to get your employement record and will give it to you a day or two from today, don't let him.  Gives him a chance to falsify and/or remove important documentation.<P>You should know the reason why you were terminated.  <P>For example, what if your manager made a pass at you, you thwarted his advance, he subsequently terminates you for that reason and subsequently puts in your folder "Reason for termination - Unreliable" when in fact you are always promt, work late and/or willing to go the extra distance when asked and/or needed (not sexually, I mean) because of lack of help.<P>EDIT:  Sorry, hit the wrong buttons again and it submitted it before I was done.<P>Anywho!  If they are ever used as a reference, although they can not legally talk negatively about your employement record  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> (at least in our state), they can impede you from future employment with falsified or incomplete records.<P>This is just food for thought.  You're still young and perhaps this really does not concern you at this time.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by JSocha (edited 08-28-2001).]||||reg||4
