Z||000013||stimpy||08-28-2001||07:53 PM||||FILE FOR UNEMPLOYMENT IMMEDIATELY!<P>If they did not give you any verbal or written warnings, they cannot contest your claim. Even if they do, appeal it and I guarantee they will not attend the hearing.  Now I'm not suggesting that you latch on to the state's bosom, but increased cost for the unemployment insurance will definately eat away at their profit margin. Hit 'em in the pocketbook. Plus it will keep your cat in Fresh Step and Whiska's...||||reg||1
Z||000014||JSocha||08-28-2001||08:30 PM||||Toys-R-Us?  You better watch out for the giraffe beater that is on this forum.  Was that not Santa Cruizer who went out of Toys-R-Us and beat up the giraffe?<P>If fierobaby was only part time, she will not get unemployment benefits.  At least in ND that is how it works.  May be different else where, don't know.  But Stimpy is right, they would not be able to contest it, especially if your state is not an "Employement at Will" state like ND is, where it can be challenged only if the employer has documented everything.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by JSocha (edited 08-28-2001).]||||reg||10
